33710-da3e7363-73d3-4643-99e6-30259e89eb45"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"bf35b18de7ec3085d30aa3bb38f499c1348b4b848e952a0a406874e47680dce6","event_uuid":"3224b0d0-70e6-463c-a2ea-36ec5611d159","position":{"commit_sha":"a92cb3c69384dc3f749ebfc3ef3d53a7e1347c9a","position":"1795087346106012284-3224b0d0-70e6-463c-a2ea-36ec5611d159"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e81be0a54fa0ae15e5ac50f656cbeba2275b62ccade12d70891b9b3bb9d38e0d","event_uuid":"392640ff-02da-4a24-8ffd-d64ebe43f38e","position":{"commit_sha":"adddb64f120018019e03788ba0d542971bf97e3b","position":"1795087543244584943-392640ff-02da-4a24-8ffd-d64ebe43f38e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The 2 `tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py::test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8` failures are owned by scholastic-travelsick-salmon (cluster A3, session 3d705fec). Root cause: on Windows, text-mode subprocess stdin turns `\\n` into `\\r\\n`, so git hashes `café ✓\\r\\n` while the test expects the LF-only bytes. The fix sends stdin without a line ending. The other 12 failures listed here are not covered by that change.","timestamp":1795087346106012284},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"12 of the 14 failures are A1 follow-ups and are fixed on branch a1-win-followup (make verify running, then Gerrit): the 5 path-separator guard tests (commit under obtuse-phenocryst-verdin) and the 7 test_uv_pin_guard cases (commit under arctic-unsecular-esok). Both are test-only and render expected paths in POSIX form. The other 2, test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8, come from 04e175d70eb (livid-painful-mosquito), not A1, and are tracked by scholastic-travelsick-salmon (CRLF on text-mode stdin, confirmed by blob hash).","timestamp":1795087543244584943}],"created_at":1795087161479914659,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fdeef63b-3124-4a91-bded-f7cb37c53dff","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"bb9f-ecd8-06dc-4521"},{"link_uuid":"99804fcd-4d8c-4800-bf8c-e6c25119361f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"453c-cad2-fab5-456d"},{"link_uuid":"da3e7363-73d3-4643-99e6-30259e89eb45","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3e8c-b2fc-d34e-4a36"}],"description":"## Observation (2026-11-19 PST)\n`test.yml` dispatched on main at `92d3f373e2c` (run 44503581058), job `sweep (windows)` 135490319213: 14 failed, 20,016 passed.\n- 12 also failed on main at `3f47117c97b` (run 44487190183, job 135433617476, 13 failures). They compare backslash paths against forward-slash expectations or vice versa:\n  - `tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py::test_exactly_one_rebar_dir_definition_under_src`\n  - `tests/unit/test_repo_root_from_package_guard.py::test_the_only_sanctioned_site_is_the_resolver_seam`\n  - `tests/unit/test_repo_root_from_tracker_guard.py` (2 tests)\n  - `tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py::test_the_argparse_positive_int_is_defined_once_and_its_namesake_survives`\n  - `tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py` (7 tests): the expected message uses `infra\\compose\\Dockerfile.svc`, while the script prints `infra/compose/Dockerfile.svc`.\n- 2 are new since `04e175d70eb` (ticket `livid-painful-mosquito`, closed): `tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py::test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8[process-group]` and `[subprocess-run]` (blob SHA mismatch on Windows, which points at a newline translation of the stdin text).\n- The previous run's one other failure, `test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py::test_write_survives_foreground_maintenance_repack` (worker crash), did not recur.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` on main passes, or each remaining failure has its own ticket; verified by the job result of a `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` dispatch.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","3e8c-b2fc-d34e-4a36"],["relates_to","453c-cad2-fab5-456d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows"],"ticket_id":"e816-b30a-6a5c-4ae4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep on main fails 14 tests: path separators in guard tests, uv-pin messages, and the new run_git stdin encoding test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["33b1ba65-c56d-4298-9652-a324867e6d3f","fdeef63b-3124-4a91-bded-f7cb37c53dff","99804fcd-4d8c-4800-bf8c-e6c25119361f","da3e7363-73d3-4643-99e6-30259e89eb45","3224b0d0-70e6-463c-a2ea-36ec5611d159","392640ff-02da-4a24-8ffd-d64ebe43f38e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795087543244584944,"uuid":"26559987-6b5f-42f0-9e04-8c0db30d1944"}